# No line-ending conversion, on any platform: every working file is byte-for-byte the blob that
# SOURCE-MANIFEST.json hashes and that the release was built from.
* -text
# Except the batch launchers, which cmd.exe wants with CRLF: stored LF, checked out CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
# And the shell launcher, which bash wants with LF on every checkout (CRLF fails with "$'\r': command not found").
*.sh text eol=lf
# And the player's changelog, which ships as CHANGELOG.txt: CRLF, so Notepad before Windows 10 1809 (Windows 7 is
# supported) shows lines, not one run-on line. Stored LF like the batch files, so the manifest hash is unchanged.
work/CHANGELOG.md text eol=crlf
